# First Roll - BONANZA's course 1, the one Enter plays (SPEC.md 128.10.3).
# The worked example of the text format: every wave-1 rule in a minute.
# Ships: everything under apps/bonanza/courses/ is a part of BONANZA.O88.
course FIRST "First Roll"
width  64
ball   rubber
floor rect   3 4  7 7  flat 4             # A plateau, 4 x 3 tiles, 4 units (32 px) up
wall  rect   3 3  7 4  flat 6             # its back rail, 2 units (16 px) proud
floor rect   7 4 11 7  ramp x 7 11 4 2    # B falls along +wx: r = 2(2-4)/(11-7) = -1 half unit a tile
floor rect  11 4 14 7  flat 0             # C the foot: B's lip is 2 units (16 px) above it
goal  rect  13 4 14 7  flat 0             # C's last column is the goal
hole  tile  12 5                          # a pit in C
start 4 5

# Wave 4 (SPEC.md 128.14.6): the route its ROUTE DEMO is the autopilot's run on
# (128.14.7.4), along the plateau's back rail and C's back row, clear of the
# pit, to the goal column - and its par, the autopilot's time and a third
# (128.14.3.1, PROVISIONAL).
way  4 5
way 11 4
way 13 4
par  4
# Wave 5b (SPEC.md 128.15.8): the design time (CD3), the early class until its retrofit; the
# course budget reads it (6275 bytes packed, refused past 1.5 times).  Tool-only:
# it writes nothing into the part, so no identity moves.
target 30
